MuPDF 1.28.6: keep JPEG metadata warnings out of terminal output.

The metadata reader must use the same quiet libjpeg diagnostic callback as
the full decoder. libjpeg's default callback writes directly to stderr,
interleaving terminal graphics even when MuPDF callbacks are configured.

--- a/source/fitz/load-jpeg.c
+++ b/source/fitz/load-jpeg.c
@@ -529,6 +529,8 @@
 	cinfo.mem = NULL;
 	cinfo.global_state = 0;
 	cinfo.err = jpeg_std_error(&err);
+	/* ptz (2026-11-16): metadata warnings must not write to the terminal. */
+	err.output_message = output_message;
 	err.error_exit = error_exit;
 
 	cinfo.client_data = NULL;
